{
 "thread": "XzBmxspIZM0",
 "subject": "using occu() or colext() with proportions (rather than 0 vs. 1)?",
 "messages_listed": 3,
 "last_activity": "2015-06-12T13:33:58Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "PXTxYlP3aN0J",
   "from": "Giancarlo Sadoti",
   "author": "d3fd439c2e48caf1",
   "date": "2015-06-11T20:04:12Z",
   "subject": "using occu() or colext() with proportions (rather than 0 vs. 1)?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Greetings all,<br><br>My apologies if this has been asked previously (a cursory search turned up nothing), but can proportional response data be reliably modeled in occu or colext? I&#39;ve attempted this without obvious errors, but I don&#39;t have enough &quot;under-the-hood&quot; knowledge.<br><br>This kind of response is common in a standard glm with binomial error, but I imagine is unlikely when data is collected with occupancy modeling in mind. <br><br>Let&#39;s take an example: say multiple 10-minute detection/non-detection surveys within a period of closure were divided into subunits. Years later, the (summarized) data provided to the analyst was proportional (e.g. percent of 1-minute periods with detections). Of course the modeler could convert these proportions to a binary response (0 vs. &gt;0), but it would *seem* more information would be contained in the proportional data.<br><br>Thanks, as always!<br><br>Giancarlo<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "3vitTbyx0_QJ",
   "from": "Dan Linden",
   "author": "527d9b3ec7deff2d",
   "date": "2015-06-12T13:30:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: using occu() or colext() with proportions (rather than 0 vs. 1)?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Giancarlo, I can&#39;t comment on whether unmarked can handle such a response variable, but one way to trick it would be to create random capture histories for each site according to how many of the 10 intervals had a detection:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"font-family:courier new,monospace\"><span style=\"color:#000\">nsites</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>K </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rbinom</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nsites</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K  </span><span style=\"color:#800\">#simulated proportions</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> matrix</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nsites</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nsites</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prop</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]*</span><span style=\"color:#000\">K</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>head</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"border-collapse:separate;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:22px;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(225,226,229)\"><pre style=\"outline-style:none;outline-width:initial;outline-color:initial;border-style:none;border-width:initial;border-color:initial;white-space:pre-wrap!important;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.2\"><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">9</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">[,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  