r:#000\">     </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span></pre></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Obviously there are some issues with this, particularly the fact that 1-min intervals are short and likely not independent.  There is also no way to account for survey-level effects (the capture histories are by their very creation assuming independence and similarity), though you could still have site-level covariates for detection.  But this last point is no different than assuming a binomial response with K&gt;1.<br><br></div>"
